---
import SiteLayout from "../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import pages from "../../../data/pages.json";
---

<SiteLayout metadata={pages["/templates/dap-notes/"]}>
  <main id="main" class="growth-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>{" "}
        <a href="/tools/">Resources</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>{" "}
        <span aria-current="page">DAP notes, with room for your judgment.</span>
      </nav>
      <header class="growth-hero">
        <div class="eyebrow">Free documentation resource</div>
        <h1>DAP notes, with room for your judgment.</h1>
        <p>
          We use this format to show how the pieces of an encounter fit
          together. Explore a fictional example, then keep a blank template for
          your own approved workflow.
        </p>
      </header>
      <div class="growth-answer">
        <strong>At a glance</strong>
        <p>
          DAP groups the session information under Data, followed by your
          assessment and plan.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="growth-split">
        <section>
          <h2>What goes in each section?</h2>
          <div class="format-part">
            <span>D</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Data</h3>
              <p>
                The client’s report, your observations, interventions, and
                response.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="format-part">
            <span>A</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Assessment</h3>
              <p>
                Your interpretation of the session and progress toward goals.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="format-part">
            <span>P</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Plan</h3>
              <p>The agreed next steps and follow-up.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
        <aside class="growth-note">
          <span class="tag">A template to keep</span>
          <h2>Start with a blank copy.</h2>
          <p>
            Download the prompts in Otto’s document style, or try the editable
            example below.
          </p>
          <button class="button" id="note-blank">
            Download blank template ↗
          </button>
          <p class="micro">
            HTML download with embedded font and logo. Use your browser to print
            or save a PDF.
          </p>
          <a class="text-link" href="#note-builder">
            Try the template ↓
          </a>
        </aside>
      </div>
      <section class="growth-section prose">
        <h2>A fictional DAP example</h2>
        <div class="review-note">
          Educational excerpt written by Otto editorial. This is not a complete
          clinical record or an output from Otto’s AI. It omits patient
          identifiers, diagnoses, and risk findings; a real record must reflect
          the actual encounter and applicable requirements. Clinical review is
          pending.
        </div>
        <h3>Data</h3>
        <p>
          The fictional client reports completing a planned evening walk on
          three days and describes feeling more able to pause before responding
          to work messages. During the fictional session, the client identifies
          one difficult work interaction and participates in a rehearsal of a
          response they would like to try.
        </p>
        <h3>Assessment</h3>
        <p>
          The example shows the client practicing a previously discussed skill.
          A real assessment would connect the observed response to the
          established treatment goals and document the clinician’s actual
          findings.
        </p>
        <h3>Plan</h3>
        <p>
          In this fictional example, the client agrees to try the rehearsed
          response once and bring an observation to the next scheduled session.
          The clinician plans to review what happened.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section class="growth-section" id="note-builder">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">Try the structure</span>
            <h2>Make the format familiar.</h2>
          </div>
          <button class="button outline" id="note-demo">
            Fill with demo data
          </button>
        </div>
        <form id="note-form" data-format="dap">
          <div class="note-fields">
            <label>
              Data
              <textarea
                name="d"
                rows="4"
                maxlength="6000"
                placeholder="The client’s report, your observations, interventions, and response."
              ></textarea>
            </label>
            <label>
              Assessment
              <textarea
                name="a"
                rows="4"
                maxlength="6000"
                placeholder="Your interpretation of the session and progress toward goals."
              ></textarea>
            </label>
            <label>
              Plan
              <textarea
                name="p"
                rows="4"
                maxlength="6000"
                placeholder="The agreed next steps and follow-up."
              ></textarea>
            </label>
          </div>
          <div class="actions">
            <button class="button" type="button" id="note-download">
              Download draft
            </button>
            <button class="button outline" type="button" id="note-print">
              Print / save as PDF
            </button>
            <button class="button outline" type="reset">
              Clear fields
            </button>
          </div>
          <p class="micro">
            Use fictional information in this review site. Entries stay in this
            page and are cleared on reload.
          </p>
          <p id="note-status" role="status"></p>
        </form>
      </section>
      <section class="growth-section prose">
        <h2>What we check before a note is final</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            The note reflects the actual encounter and distinguishes reports,
            observations, and clinical interpretation.
          </li>
          <li>
            Relevant interventions, the client’s response, and progress toward
            treatment goals are described.
          </li>
          <li>
            Required encounter details, assessments, decisions, follow-up, and
            signature are completed through the practice’s approved workflow.
          </li>
          <li>
            Copied text is reviewed for stale details or statements unsupported
            by this visit.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Use our <a href="/blog/soap-vs-dap-notes/">SOAP-versus-DAP guide</a>{" "}
          to compare the structures, or explore{" "}
          <a href="/ai-progress-notes/">Otto’s AI note workflow</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section class="otto-tool-hook" aria-label="Meet Otto">
        <div class="otto-hook-mark" aria-hidden="true">
          <img src="/assets/otto-logo.svg" alt="" />
          <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100">
            <path d="M50 100V25" stroke="#004852" stroke-width="2" />
            <path d="M50 75C13 73 8 43 8 33c31 1 42 20 42 42" fill="#8ca7a2" />
            <path d="M50 58c34-2 42-28 43-40-29 0-43 18-43 40" fill="#417e86" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="otto-hook-copy">
          <span class="eyebrow">Meet Otto by Tebra</span>
          <h2>Let Otto take more off your plate.</h2>
          <p>
            Otto drafts progress notes for your review and brings scheduling,
            telehealth, and payments into one place.
          </p>
          <div class="otto-hook-features">
            <span>AI-assisted notes</span>
            <span>Scheduling</span>
            <span>Payments</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="otto-hook-action">
          <a class="button light" href="/waitlist/">
            Learn more <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
          <span>Join the Otto waitlist</span>
        </div>
      </section>
      <div class="sources">
        <h2>Sources and review</h2>
        <p>
          Sources checked October 16, 2026. Confirm current product terms before
          choosing software.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <a href="https://www.simplepractice.com/resource/soap-note-examples/">
              SOAP format overview
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://www.mentalyc.com/blog/dap-notes">
              DAP format overview
            </a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <template id="note-blank-document">
        <article class="doc">
          <h2 class="document-title">DAP note template</h2>
          <p class="document-subtitle">
            Educational template · Complete and review through your approved
            clinical workflow.
          </p>
          <h2>Encounter details</h2>
          <p>
            [Client identifier, date, service, time, modality, clinician, and
            other required details.]
          </p>
          <h2>Data</h2>
          <p>
            [The client’s report, your observations, interventions, and
            response.]
          </p>
          <h2>Assessment</h2>
          <p>[Your interpretation of the session and progress toward goals.]</p>
          <h2>Plan</h2>
          <p>[The agreed next steps and follow-up.]</p>
          <h2>Review and signature</h2>
          <p>
            [Complete required review, clinician signature, credentials, and
            date.]
          </p>
          <p>
            Template prompts do not establish clinical completeness, medical
            necessity, or payer acceptance.
          </p>
        </article>
      </template>
      <script is:inline src="/assets/documents.js"></script>
      <script is:inline src="/assets/note-template.js" defer></script>
    </div>
    <section class="cta-section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="cta">
          <div>
            <h2>Make more room for the work you love.</h2>
            <p>
              See how Otto brings notes, scheduling, telehealth, and payments
              into your practice day.
            </p>
          </div>
          <a class="button light" href="/waitlist/">
            Join the waitlist <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
